    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d408">

                <pb facs="0436" n="360" sameAs="frus:frus1916/pg360"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 838.00/1408</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Chargé Scholle to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Port au Prince</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-09-04T14:00:00-04:49">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">September 4, 1916, 2 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Since the civil officials under the treaty have assumed office, does the
                    Department wish all Federal civil administrations now conducted by order of the
                    President turned over to the Haitian Government beginning October first?
                    Arrangements have been made with the Haitian Government for the continuation of
                    work by occupation till October first. Expeditionary commander believes it
                    necessary to retain control of hospitals, prisons, and charities to insure
                    proper maintenance.</p>
                <p>On account of health of American troops, sanitation should be retained by
                    occupation until sanitary engineer is appointed and installed.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Scholle</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
